      "content": "That's an interesting breakdown. I'm particularly interested in how the staff should handle Profile A. You mentioned they might be trying to \"blend in with wealth\" while being potentially involved in things like money laundering or smuggling. \n\nIn a high-end Dubai setting, there's a lot of nuance. On one hand, you have genuine \"new money\" or tourists who are just very loud and flashy. On the other, you have certain demographics that might be more prone to that kind of \"trying too hard\" behavior. \n\nTo help the staff be more precise, could you expand on the specific traits that distinguish a group of genuine, albeit loud, wealthy tourists from a group that is a genuine security risk? For example, when looking at their language, physical mannerisms, or even the specific type of \"flashy\" brands they wear, are there certain patterns that are more statistically associated with criminal intent in luxury hospitality environments?",
